IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `qsa-dates`

-- Succession Act 1981 (Qld) -- the rules a person with a claim on a deceased person's estate meets: who is a spouse
-- (s 5AA) and an unborn child (s 5A); the will a claimant may rely on or challenge (ss 9, 10, 11, 12, 14, 14A, 15, 15A,
-- 15B, 18, 33, 33B, 33Z); distribution on intestacy (Part 3: ss 34A, 35, 36, 36A, 37, 39A, 39B and schedule 2); family
-- provision (Part 4: ss 40, 40A, 41, 44, with s 5B); survivorship (s 65); and the survival of actions for or against an
-- estate (s 66).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in qsa-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and never restates a rule.
-- Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("means", "only if", "is not
-- valid", "is revoked", "is void", "shall not", "may only be made within", an "if" condition that fails); or NOTHING
-- where the Act does not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. The court's judgments ("satisfied",
-- "adequate provision", "proper", "just and equitable", "appropriate") are inputs: the answer is conditional on them,
-- never a guess at them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) The State of Queensland,
-- CC BY 4.0; not the authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See
-- NOTES.md.

§ `Succession Act 1981`

§§ `The time limits, as a duty to act in time`

-- "may only be made within" (s 33(2)), "shall not be heard ... unless ... instituted within" (s 41(8)), "must be made
-- within" (s 39A(3)): what the person in the seat must do to keep the step open. The rule starts on a day and allows the
-- days to the last day; FULFILLED means in time and anything else too late. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never
-- exported.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the person in the seat`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `take the step`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`the step must be taken within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the person in the seat`
    MUST `take the step`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person in the seat` BECAUSE "the time the Succession Act 1981 allows for this step has run out"

GIVEN `the time of the step` IS A NUMBER, `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `taking the step at` `the time of the step` `keeps` `the rule` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time of the step`), (EVENT `the person in the seat` `take the step` `the time of the step`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Whether a step taken on a day is in time where the last day is fixed. The rule is started on the earlier of the two
-- days, so that a step taken before the start of counting is in time.
GIVEN `the day of the step` IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a step on` `the day of the step` `is in time for the last day` `the last day` IF
    `taking the step at` (`the number of days from` `the base` `until` `the day of the step`) `keeps` (`the step must be taken within` (`the number of days from` `the base` `until` `the last day`))
    WHERE
        `the base` MEANS `the earlier day of` `the day of the step` `and` `the last day`

§§ `s 5AA -- who is the spouse of a deceased person`

DECLARE `Relationship with the deceased at the death` IS ONE OF
    `husband or wife`
    `civil partner`
    `de facto partner`
    `former husband or wife, divorced from the deceased`
    `former civil partner, the civil partnership terminated under the Civil Partnerships Act 2011 s 19`
    `none of these`

-- s 5AA(2): "a person is a spouse of a deceased person only if, on the deceased's death -- (a) the person was the
-- deceased's husband or wife; or (b) ... de facto partner ... [and] had lived together as a couple on a genuine
-- domestic basis ... for a continuous period of at least 2 years ending on the deceased's death; or (ba) ... civil
-- partner; or (c) for part 4, ... (ii) the deceased's dependant former husband or wife or civil partner." s 5AA(4): a
-- dependent former spouse or civil partner had not remarried or entered into a civil partnership (or, for a civil
-- partner, married or entered into another civil partnership) before the death, and was on the death "receiving, or
-- entitled to receive, maintenance from the deceased". "only if": JUST FALSE when no limb holds. "De facto partner" and
-- "lived together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis" are borrowed from the Acts Interpretation Act 1954 s 32DA and
-- asked as facts.
GIVEN `the relationship` IS A `Relationship with the deceased at the death`, `lived together for 2 years ending on the death` IS A BOOLEAN, `for family provision` IS A BOOLEAN, `remarried or partnered before the death` IS A BOOLEAN, `receiving or entitled to maintenance at the death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5AA -- I am the spouse of the deceased` `the relationship` `lived together for 2 years ending on the death` `for family provision` `remarried or partnered before the death` `receiving or entitled to maintenance at the death` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the relationship`
    WHEN `husband or wife` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `civil partner` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `de facto partner` THEN
        IF `lived together for 2 years ending on the death`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `none of these` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        IF `for family provision` AND (NOT `remarried or partnered before the death`) AND `receiving or entitled to maintenance at the death`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 5A -- a child not yet born at the death`

-- s 5A: a reference to a child or issue "includes a child or issue en ventre sa mere at the death, provided such child
-- or issue is born alive and remains alive for a period of 30 days". "provided": a condition the text states, JUST FALSE
-- when it fails. "Remains alive for a period of 30 days" is read as alive throughout the 30 days after the day of birth,
-- so a child who dies on the 30th day after birth does not count (fork F3).
GIVEN `born alive` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day of birth` IS A DATE, `the child has died` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day of the child's death or today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5A -- the child unborn at the death counts` `born alive` `the day of birth` `the child has died` `the day of the child's death or today` MEANS
    IF (NOT `born alive`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the number of days from` `the day of birth` `until` `the day of the child's death or today` AT LEAST 31
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `the child has died`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: not yet known; the 30 days have not run

§§ `ss 9, 10, 18 -- whether a document is the deceased's will`

-- The facts about one document.
DECLARE `The will document` HAS
    `made while the testator was a minor`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a s 9(2) or (3) exception covers the minor's will`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `made under a s 21 order`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `in writing`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed by the testator or at the testator's direction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed with the intention of executing the will`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `witnesses present together at the signing`            IS A NUMBER
    `witnesses who attested and signed in the testator's presence` IS A NUMBER
    `states the deceased's testamentary intentions`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court is satisfied the deceased intended it as the will` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 10(2)-(4), (7), (8), (10): "A will must be -- (a) in writing; and (b) signed by -- (i) the testator; or (ii) someone
-- else, in the presence of and at the direction of the testator"; "The signature must be made or acknowledged by the
-- testator in the presence of 2 or more witnesses present at the same time"; "At least 2 of the witnesses must attest and
-- sign the will in the presence of the testator"; the signature "must be made with the intention of executing the
-- will"; a person who cannot see and attest that the testator has signed "may not act as a witness" (so only witnesses
-- who could see are counted). s 10(13): the section "does not apply to a will made under an order under section 21".
GIVEN w IS A `The will document`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10 -- the will was executed as the section requires` w IF
        w's `in writing`
    AND w's `signed by the testator or at the testator's direction`
    AND w's `signed with the intention of executing the will`
    AND w's `witnesses present together at the signing` AT LEAST 2
    AND w's `witnesses who attested and signed in the testator's presence` AT LEAST 2

-- s 9(1): "A will made by a minor is not valid", except under s 9(2) (made in contemplation of a marriage that takes
-- place; made while married; a revocation after the marriage ends) and s 9(3) (a s 19 order; s 33X). s 18(2): a
-- document that purports to state the deceased's testamentary intentions and was not executed under the Part "forms a
-- will ... if the court is satisfied that the person intended the document ... to form the person's will". A minor's will
-- is not saved by s 18 (fork F4). A s 21 will (statutory will for a person without capacity) is outside this encoding.
GIVEN w IS A `The will document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 9, 10, 18 -- the document is the deceased's will` w MEANS
    IF w's `made while the testator was a minor` AND (NOT w's `a s 9(2) or (3) exception covers the minor's will`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF w's `made under a s 21 order`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: outside this encoding (s 21 statutory wills, Part 2 division 4 subdivision 3)
         ELSE IF `s 10 -- the will was executed as the section requires` w
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE IF (NOT w's `states the deceased's testamentary intentions`)
                   THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: silent; s 18 reaches only a document that purports to state testamentary intentions
                   ELSE IF w's `the court is satisfied the deceased intended it as the will`
                        THEN JUST TRUE
                        ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 11, 12 -- a gift to a witness or an interpreter`

DECLARE `My part in making the will` IS ONE OF
    `an attesting witness`
    `the interpreter or translator for the will`

-- s 11(2): a disposition to an attesting witness "is void to the extent it concerns the interested witness", but not if
-- (3)(a) at least 2 of the attesting witnesses are not interested witnesses, (b) all who would benefit from the avoidance
-- consent in writing with capacity, or (c) the court is satisfied the testator knew and approved and it was made freely
-- and voluntarily. s 12(2), (3): the same for an interpreter, with (3)(a) and (b) matching s 11(3)(b) and (c). ss 11(4),
-- 12(4): a direction to pay a debt or appropriate remuneration is not a "disposition of property". Answers whether I keep
-- the gift: JUST FALSE where it is void.
GIVEN `my part` IS A `My part in making the will`, `the gift is only a debt or appropriate remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN, `attesting witnesses who are not interested` IS A NUMBER, `all who would benefit consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court is satisfied the testator knew and approved freely` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 11, 12 -- I keep the gift` `my part` `the gift is only a debt or appropriate remuneration` `attesting witnesses who are not interested` `all who would benefit consented in writing` `the court is satisfied the testator knew and approved freely` MEANS
    IF `the gift is only a debt or appropriate remuneration` OR `all who would benefit consented in writing` OR `the court is satisfied the testator knew and approved freely`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `my part`
         WHEN `an attesting witness` THEN
             IF `attesting witnesses who are not interested` AT LEAST 2
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE
         WHEN `the interpreter or translator for the will` THEN JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 14, 14A -- the testator's later marriage or civil partnership`

DECLARE `The testator's later union` IS ONE OF
    `the testator married`
    `the testator entered into a civil partnership`

DECLARE `What the will says it contemplates` IS ONE OF
    `marriage generally`
    `a civil partnership generally`
    `neither`

-- s 14(1): "A will is revoked by the marriage of the testator"; s 14A(1): "... by the testator entering into a civil
-- partnership". Not revoked: (2)(a) a disposition to, and (b) an appointment of, the person the testator is married to
-- (in a civil partnership with) at death; (3)(a) a will made in contemplation of that marriage (civil partnership),
-- stated or not; (3)(b) a will "stated to be made in contemplation of marriage generally" (s 14A: "of a civil
-- partnership generally") is not revoked by a marriage (civil partnership). A marriage before the will was made does not
-- revoke it. The s 14(2)(c), s 14A(2)(c) powers of appointment are out. Answers whether my gift or appointment stands.
GIVEN `the union` IS A `The testator's later union`, `it came after the will` IS A BOOLEAN, `the gift is to the testator's spouse or civil partner at death` IS A BOOLEAN, `the will was made in contemplation of that union` IS A BOOLEAN, `the will states it contemplates` IS A `What the will says it contemplates`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 14, 14A -- my gift survives the testator's later union` `the union` `it came after the will` `the gift is to the testator's spouse or civil partner at death` `the will was made in contemplation of that union` `the will states it contemplates` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it came after the will`) OR `the gift is to the testator's spouse or civil partner at death` OR `the will was made in contemplation of that union` OR `generally contemplated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `generally contemplated` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the union`
            WHEN `the testator married` THEN
                CONSIDER `the will states it contemplates`
                WHEN `marriage generally` THEN TRUE
                OTHERWISE FALSE
            WHEN `the testator entered into a civil partnership` THEN
                CONSIDER `the will states it contemplates`
                WHEN `a civil partnership generally` THEN TRUE
                OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 15, 15A, 15B -- divorce, annulment, the end of a civil partnership or of a de facto relationship`

DECLARE `What the will gave me` IS ONE OF
    `a gift of property`
    `an appointment as executor, trustee, advisory trustee or guardian`
    `an appointment as trustee of property left on trust for beneficiaries that include my children`
    `a power of appointment I may exercise only in favour of children of whom the testator and I are both parents`
    `another power of appointment exercisable by me or in my favour`

-- s 15(1) (15A(1), 15B(1)): the divorce or annulment (termination or void finding, end of the de facto relationship)
-- "revokes -- (a) a disposition to the testator's former spouse made by a will in existence when the divorce or
-- annulment happens; and (b) an appointment ... as an executor, trustee, advisory trustee or guardian; and (c) any grant
-- ... of a power of appointment exercisable by, or in favour of," the former spouse. (2): it "does not revoke" (a) an
-- appointment as trustee of property on trust for beneficiaries that include the former spouse's children, or (b) a
-- power exercisable by the former spouse only in favour of their common children. (3): "Subsection (1) does not apply if
-- a contrary intention appears in the will." (4): the will then takes effect as if the former spouse died before the
-- testator. A will made after the ending is not revoked (fork F5). Answers whether my gift or appointment stands.
GIVEN `what I got` IS A `What the will gave me`, `the will existed when it ended` IS A BOOLEAN, `a contrary intention appears in the will` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 15, 15A, 15B -- my gift survives the end of our relationship` `what I got` `the will existed when it ended` `a contrary intention appears in the will` MEANS
    IF `a contrary intention appears in the will` OR (NOT `the will existed when it ended`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `what I got`
         WHEN `an appointment as trustee of property left on trust for beneficiaries that include my children` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a power of appointment I may exercise only in favour of children of whom the testator and I are both parents` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 33 -- rectifying a will`

-- s 33(2): "An application for an order to rectify a will may only be made within 6 months after the date of death of
-- the testator." (3): the court may at any time extend the time if it considers it appropriate and the final
-- distribution of the estate has not been made.
GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 33(2) -- the last day to apply to rectify` `the day of death` MEANS `the day` 6 `months after` `the day of death`

GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE, `the day of applying` IS A DATE, `the court extends the time` IS A BOOLEAN, `the final distribution has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33 -- my application to rectify may be made` `the day of death` `the day of applying` `the court extends the time` `the final distribution has been made` MEANS
    IF `a step on` `the day of applying` `is in time for the last day` (`s 33(2) -- the last day to apply to rectify` `the day of death`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the court extends the time` AND (NOT `the final distribution has been made`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 33B, s 35(2) -- surviving the deceased by 30 days`

DECLARE `How the person takes` IS ONE OF
    `under the will`
    `on intestacy`

-- s 33B(1): "If a disposition of property is made to a person who dies within 30 days after the testator's death, the
-- will takes effect as if the person had died immediately before the testator." (2), (3): not if a contrary intention
-- appears in the will; a general requirement to survive the testator is not one. s 35(2): a person entitled on intestacy
-- who "does not survive the intestate for a period of 30 days" is treated as having died before the intestate. Both are
-- read as: the person takes only if alive throughout the 30 days after the day of the death, so a death on the 30th day
-- after fails and one on the 31st takes (fork F3). A person who died on or before the day of the death: under a will the
-- general law of lapse and s 33N govern (NOTHING); on intestacy the person did not survive (JUST FALSE).
GIVEN `how` IS A `How the person takes`, `the day the deceased died` IS A DATE, `the day the person died` IS A DATE, `a contrary intention appears in the will` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 33B, 35(2) -- the person who died soon after still takes` `how` `the day the deceased died` `the day the person died` `a contrary intention appears in the will` MEANS
    IF `the gap` AT LEAST 31
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `how`
         WHEN `on intestacy` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `under the will` THEN
             IF `the gap` AT MOST 0
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: points outside the text (the general law of lapse; s 33N for issue)
             ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears in the will`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the gap` MEANS `the number of days from` `the day the deceased died` `until` `the day the person died`

§§ `s 33Z -- seeing a copy of the will`

DECLARE `Who I am to the will` IS ONE OF
    `a person mentioned in the will`
    `a beneficiary under an earlier will of the testator`
    `the testator's spouse, parent or issue`
    `a person who would share in the estate on an intestacy`
    `the parent or guardian of a minor mentioned in the will or who would share on an intestacy`
    `a creditor or other person with a claim at law or in equity against the estate`
    `a person who may apply for family provision under s 41`
    `none of these`

-- s 33Z(1), (2): a person with possession or control of a will (or, if it is lost, stolen or destroyed, a copy) of a
-- deceased testator "must, if asked" allow "an entitled person" to inspect it and give a certified copy on payment of
-- reasonable expenses. s 33Z(4): "entitled person ... means" (a)-(g). "means": JUST FALSE for anyone else.
GIVEN `who I am` IS A `Who I am to the will`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33Z -- I am entitled to inspect and copy the will` `who I am` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who I am`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 34A -- household chattels`

DECLARE `Kind of item` IS ONE OF
    `furniture, curtains, carpets, linen, china, glassware, ornaments, or domestic or garden appliances, utensils or effects`
    `liquor, wine or consumable stores`
    `a domestic animal`
    `another chattel of ordinary household use or decoration`
    `a motor vehicle, boat or aircraft`
    `a racing animal`
    `an original painting or other original work of art`
    `a trophy, clothing, jewellery or other chattel of a personal nature`

-- s 34A(1): "Household chattels means" the listed things "owned by the intestate immediately before the intestate's
-- death"; (2) "does not include" a motor vehicle, boat, aircraft, racing animal, original work of art, trophy,
-- clothing, jewellery or other chattel of a personal nature; (3) a thing held subject to a security interest or under a
-- hire-purchase agreement counts as owned. "means", "does not include": JUST FALSE outside.
GIVEN `the item` IS A `Kind of item`, `owned by the intestate immediately before the death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34A -- the item is a household chattel` `the item` `owned by the intestate immediately before the death` MEANS
    IF (NOT `owned by the intestate immediately before the death`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the item`
         WHEN `a motor vehicle, boat or aircraft` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `a racing animal` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `an original painting or other original work of art` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `a trophy, clothing, jewellery or other chattel of a personal nature` THEN JUST FALSE
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part 3 and schedule 2 -- who takes on intestacy`

-- The intestate's family, counting only those who survived the intestate by 30 days (s 35(2)), with a child born after
-- the death counted under s 5A; half-blood relatives count as whole-blood ones (s 34(2)).
DECLARE `The intestate's family` HAS
    `surviving spouses`                                     IS A NUMBER
    `children who survived`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `children who died before, leaving issue who survived`  IS A NUMBER
    `parents who survived`                                  IS A NUMBER
    `brothers and sisters who survived`                     IS A NUMBER
    `brothers and sisters who died before, leaving children who survived` IS A NUMBER
    `grandparents who survived`                             IS A NUMBER
    `uncles and aunts who survived`                         IS A NUMBER
    `uncles and aunts who died before, leaving children who survived` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Who takes the residuary estate` IS ONE OF
    `the spouse or spouses alone`
    `the spouse or spouses, and the issue`
    `the issue`
    `the parents`
    `the brothers and sisters, and children of those who died`
    `the grandparents`
    `the uncles and aunts, and children of those who died`
    `the Crown, as bona vacantia`

GIVEN f IS A `The intestate's family`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the branches of issue in` f MEANS f's `children who survived` PLUS f's `children who died before, leaving issue who survived`

-- Schedule 2: part 1 (survived by a spouse) items 1 and 2; part 2 (no spouse) items 1 to 4; s 37(1)(a)-(c) for the
-- order among the next of kin (s 35(1A)).
GIVEN f IS A `The intestate's family`
GIVETH A `Who takes the residuary estate`
`schedule 2 -- who takes` f MEANS
    IF f's `surviving spouses` AT LEAST 1
    THEN IF `the branches of issue in` f AT LEAST 1
         THEN `the spouse or spouses, and the issue`
         ELSE `the spouse or spouses alone`
    ELSE IF `the branches of issue in` f AT LEAST 1
         THEN `the issue`
         ELSE IF f's `parents who survived` AT LEAST 1
              THEN `the parents`
              ELSE IF f's `brothers and sisters who survived` PLUS f's `brothers and sisters who died before, leaving children who survived` AT LEAST 1
                   THEN `the brothers and sisters, and children of those who died`
                   ELSE IF f's `grandparents who survived` AT LEAST 1
                        THEN `the grandparents`
                        ELSE IF f's `uncles and aunts who survived` PLUS f's `uncles and aunts who died before, leaving children who survived` AT LEAST 1
                             THEN `the uncles and aunts, and children of those who died`
                             ELSE `the Crown, as bona vacantia`

-- Schedule 2, part 1, item 2: the spouse (or the spouses together, under s 36) take "$150,000 and the household
-- chattels; and (b) the following part of the residuary estate then remaining -- (i) if there is only 1 child of the
-- intestate who survived, or who did not survive but left issue who survived, the intestate -- 1/2; (ii) otherwise --
-- 1/3." The value here leaves out the household chattels, which the spouse takes in kind.
GIVEN `the residue` IS A NUMBER, f IS A `The intestate's family`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`schedule 2 part 1 item 2 -- the spouses' part of` `the residue` `for` f MEANS
    min `the residue` 150000 PLUS (`the fraction` TIMES max 0 (`the residue` MINUS 150000))
    WHERE
        `the fraction` MEANS
            IF `the branches of issue in` f EQUALS 1
            THEN 1/2
            ELSE 1/3

DECLARE `My place in the intestate's family` IS ONE OF
    `a spouse`
    `a child`
    `a grandchild or other issue, whose parent (the intestate's child) died before`
    `a parent`
    `a brother or sister`
    `a child of a brother or sister who died before`
    `a grandparent`
    `an uncle or aunt`
    `a child of an uncle or aunt who died before`
    `a more remote relative`

-- s 36A(3)-(7) (and s 37(2), which divides among the next of kin as if they were children and grandchildren): the
-- amount is divided into as many equal shares as there are members of the class who survived or who died before leaving
-- issue (children, for s 37) who survived; a surviving member takes one share; the share of a member who died is taken
-- "by representation" by that member's surviving issue. The asker who takes through a member who died gives the number
-- of shares that member's share is divided into (fork F6). Answers NOTHING where the asker's place does not fit the
-- counts given.
GIVEN `the amount` IS A NUMBER, `members who survived` IS A NUMBER, `members who died leaving issue` IS A NUMBER, `I am a member` IS A BOOLEAN, `I take through a member who died` IS A BOOLEAN, `the shares in my branch` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the share by representation of` `the amount` `among` `members who survived` `and` `members who died leaving issue` `as member` `I am a member` `as issue of one who died` `I take through a member who died` `in a branch of` `the shares in my branch` MEANS
    IF `I am a member`
    THEN IF `members who survived` AT LEAST 1
         THEN JUST (`the amount` DIVIDED BY (`members who survived` PLUS `members who died leaving issue`))
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: the facts given do not fit (no member survived)
    ELSE IF `I take through a member who died`
         THEN IF `members who died leaving issue` AT LEAST 1 AND `the shares in my branch` AT LEAST 1
              THEN JUST (`the amount` DIVIDED BY (`members who survived` PLUS `members who died leaving issue`) DIVIDED BY `the shares in my branch`)
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: the facts given do not fit
         ELSE JUST 0

-- The spouse's share: the whole part if there is one spouse; with more than one, s 36 decides (an agreement, a court
-- order, or the personal representative's equal division under s 36(1)(c)); only an equal division is answered.
GIVEN `the part` IS A NUMBER, `spouses` IS A NUMBER, `shared equally` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the spouse's share of` `the part` `among` `spouses` `spouses, equally` `shared equally` MEANS
    IF `spouses` EQUALS 1
    THEN JUST `the part`
    ELSE IF `shared equally`
         THEN JUST (`the part` DIVIDED BY `spouses`)
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: s 36 leaves the division to an agreement or a court order

-- s 35(1) and schedule 2: my share of the residuary estate, in money, leaving out the household chattels (which go to the
-- spouse, or are shared like the rest where there is none). Subject to any family provision order (s 34(3)).
GIVEN `my place` IS A `My place in the intestate's family`, f IS A `The intestate's family`, `the residue` IS A NUMBER, `the shares in my branch` IS A NUMBER, `the spouses share equally` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 35, schedule 2 -- my share of the residuary estate` `my place` f `the residue` `the shares in my branch` `the spouses share equally` MEANS
    CONSIDER `schedule 2 -- who takes` f
    WHEN `the spouse or spouses alone` THEN
        CONSIDER `my place`
        WHEN `a spouse` THEN `the spouse's share of` `the residue` `among` (f's `surviving spouses`) `spouses, equally` `the spouses share equally`
        OTHERWISE JUST 0
    WHEN `the spouse or spouses, and the issue` THEN
        CONSIDER `my place`
        WHEN `a spouse` THEN `the spouse's share of` `the spouses' part` `among` (f's `surviving spouses`) `spouses, equally` `the spouses share equally`
        OTHERWISE `the issue's share of` (`the residue` MINUS `the spouses' part`)
    WHEN `the issue` THEN `the issue's share of` `the residue`
    WHEN `the parents` THEN
        CONSIDER `my place`
        WHEN `a parent` THEN JUST (`the residue` DIVIDED BY f's `parents who survived`)
        OTHERWISE JUST 0
    WHEN `the brothers and sisters, and children of those who died` THEN
        `the share by representation of` `the residue` `among` (f's `brothers and sisters who survived`) `and` (f's `brothers and sisters who died before, leaving children who survived`) `as member` (`my place` EQUALS `a brother or sister`) `as issue of one who died` (`my place` EQUALS `a child of a brother or sister who died before`) `in a branch of` `the shares in my branch`
    WHEN `the grandparents` THEN
        CONSIDER `my place`
        WHEN `a grandparent` THEN JUST (`the residue` DIVIDED BY f's `grandparents who survived`)
        OTHERWISE JUST 0
    WHEN `the uncles and aunts, and children of those who died` THEN
        `the share by representation of` `the residue` `among` (f's `uncles and aunts who survived`) `and` (f's `uncles and aunts who died before, leaving children who survived`) `as member` (`my place` EQUALS `an uncle or aunt`) `as issue of one who died` (`my place` EQUALS `a child of an uncle or aunt who died before`) `in a branch of` `the shares in my branch`
    WHEN `the Crown, as bona vacantia` THEN JUST 0
    WHERE
        `the spouses' part` MEANS `schedule 2 part 1 item 2 -- the spouses' part of` `the residue` `for` f
        `the issue's share of` `the amount` MEANS
            `the share by representation of` `the amount` `among` (f's `children who survived`) `and` (f's `children who died before, leaving issue who survived`) `as member` (`my place` EQUALS `a child`) `as issue of one who died` (`my place` EQUALS `a grandchild or other issue, whose parent (the intestate's child) died before`) `in a branch of` `the shares in my branch`

§§ `s 36 -- more than one spouse`

-- s 36(1)(c): the spouses' entitlement is distributed "in equal shares as decided by the personal representative, if,
-- at the time of distribution -- (i) the spouses have been given a notice under subsection (3) and 3 months have passed
-- since the last of the notices was given; and (ii) the personal representative has no notice of a distribution
-- agreement; and (iii) the personal representative -- (A) has no notice of an application for a distribution order; or
-- (B) has been notified in writing by the spouses that [it] may distribute their entitlement equally ...; or (C) has a
-- copy of an order of the court striking out or discontinuing an application". "if": JUST FALSE when a condition fails.
-- "3 months have passed" is read as: the distribution falls after the day 3 months after the last notice (fork F7).
GIVEN `the notices were given` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day the last notice was given` IS A DATE, `the day the entitlement is distributed` IS A DATE, `notice of a distribution agreement` IS A BOOLEAN, `notice of an application for a distribution order` IS A BOOLEAN, `the spouses agreed in writing to an equal division` IS A BOOLEAN, `the application was struck out or discontinued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 36(1)(c) -- the personal representative may divide our entitlement equally` `the notices were given` `the day the last notice was given` `the day the entitlement is distributed` `notice of a distribution agreement` `notice of an application for a distribution order` `the spouses agreed in writing to an equal division` `the application was struck out or discontinued` MEANS
    IF      `the notices were given`
        AND `the day the entitlement is distributed` `falls after` (`the day` 3 `months after` `the day the last notice was given`)
        AND (NOT `notice of a distribution agreement`)
        AND (    (NOT `notice of an application for a distribution order`)
              OR `the spouses agreed in writing to an equal division`
              OR `the application was struck out or discontinued`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 39A, 39B -- the spouse's election to acquire the shared home`

-- s 39A(1), (2): where the intestate's interest in a shared home is not effectively disposed of by a will and the
-- intestate's spouse "ordinarily resided in the shared home" at the death, the spouse "may, by written notice, elect to
-- acquire the intestate's interest ... at transfer value", subject to s 39B. s 39B(1), (2): where (a) the home is part of
-- a building and the estate includes the whole building, (b) the home is part of land partly or wholly used for
-- agricultural purposes and the estate includes the whole interest, (c) the home is part of a hotel, motel, boarding
-- house or hostel, or (d) part of the home was used for non-domestic purposes, the spouse "may make an election ... only
-- if the court makes an order allowing the election". "applies if", "only if": JUST FALSE when they fail.
GIVEN `the interest is not effectively disposed of by a will` IS A BOOLEAN, `I am the spouse and ordinarily resided there at the death` IS A BOOLEAN, `a s 39B(1) circumstance applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court has ordered that I may elect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 39A, 39B -- I may elect to acquire the shared home` `the interest is not effectively disposed of by a will` `I am the spouse and ordinarily resided there at the death` `a s 39B(1) circumstance applies` `the court has ordered that I may elect` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the interest is not effectively disposed of by a will`) OR (NOT `I am the spouse and ordinarily resided there at the death`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `a s 39B(1) circumstance applies` AND (NOT `the court has ordered that I may elect`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Shared home time` IS ONE OF
    `elect by` HAS `the last day to elect` IS A DATE
    `first apply to the court for an order allowing the election, by` HAS `the last day to apply` IS A DATE
    `the 3 months have not started: the personal representative has not given the notice`

-- s 39A(3): the election "must be made -- (a) if the resident is a personal representative -- within 3 months after the
-- resident's appointment ...; or (b) if [not] -- within 3 months after the personal representative gives the resident a
-- written notice" in the terms of (3)(b)(i), (ii). s 39B(4): the application for the court's order must be made within
-- the same 3 months. s 39B(6): if the court makes the order, "the time for making the election under section 39A is
-- extended until 1 month after the order is made" (read as the later of the two days: fork F8).
GIVEN `I am a personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN, `I was given the notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day of my appointment or of the notice` IS A DATE, `a s 39B(1) circumstance applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court has ordered that I may elect` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day of the order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Shared home time`
`ss 39A(3), 39B(4), (6) -- my time to elect` `I am a personal representative` `I was given the notice` `the day of my appointment or of the notice` `a s 39B(1) circumstance applies` `the court has ordered that I may elect` `the day of the order` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I am a personal representative`) AND (NOT `I was given the notice`)
    THEN `the 3 months have not started: the personal representative has not given the notice`
    ELSE IF `a s 39B(1) circumstance applies`
         THEN IF `the court has ordered that I may elect`
              THEN `elect by` (`the later day of` `three months on` `and` (`the day` 1 `months after` `the day of the order`))
              ELSE `first apply to the court for an order allowing the election, by` `three months on`
         ELSE `elect by` `three months on`
    WHERE
        `three months on` MEANS `the day` 3 `months after` `the day of my appointment or of the notice`

-- Whether an election given on a day is in time. "must be made within": JUST FALSE once the time has run, or while a
-- needed court order has not been made (s 39B(2), "only if"); NOTHING before the 3 months have started (NOTHING-kind:
-- silent; s 39A(3)(b) counts only from the notice).
GIVEN `the day of electing` IS A DATE, `the time` IS A `Shared home time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39A(3) -- an election on` `the day of electing` `is in time under` `the time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the time`
    WHEN `elect by` `the final day` THEN
        IF `a step on` `the day of electing` `is in time for the last day` `the final day`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `first apply to the court for an order allowing the election, by` `the final day` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `the 3 months have not started: the personal representative has not given the notice` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: silent; the 3 months run only from the notice (fork F2)

§§ `s 40, s 40A -- child, stepchild and dependant`

-- s 40: "dependant means ... any person who was being wholly or substantially maintained or supported (otherwise than
-- for full valuable consideration) by that deceased person at the time of the person's death being -- (a) a parent of
-- that deceased person; or (b) the parent of a surviving child under the age of 18 years of that deceased person; or (c)
-- a person under the age of 18 years." "means": JUST FALSE outside it.
GIVEN `maintained by the deceased at the death` IS A BOOLEAN, `a parent of the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN, `a parent of a surviving child of the deceased under 18` IS A BOOLEAN, `under 18 at the death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40 -- I am a dependant of the deceased` `maintained by the deceased at the death` `a parent of the deceased` `a parent of a surviving child of the deceased under 18` `under 18 at the death` MEANS
    IF `maintained by the deceased at the death` AND (`a parent of the deceased` OR `a parent of a surviving child of the deceased under 18` OR `under 18 at the death`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `My parent and the deceased` IS ONE OF
    `my parent was the deceased's spouse when the deceased died`
    `their marriage, civil partnership or de facto relationship lasted until my parent died, before the deceased`
    `their marriage, civil partnership or de facto relationship ended in divorce, termination or separation`
    `my parent was never the deceased's spouse`

-- s 40A(1): a stepchild is "the child of a spouse of the deceased person" whose step-relationship did not stop under
-- (2) (divorce, termination of the civil partnership, the end of the de facto relationship). (3)(a): it does not stop
-- because the parent died first while the relationship subsisted, nor (3)(b) because the deceased later re-partnered.
-- "if": JUST FALSE outside. A parent who died first is not a "spouse" on the deceased's death under s 5AA(2); s 40A(3)(a)
-- is followed (fork F9, finding 2).
GIVEN `my parent and the deceased` IS A `My parent and the deceased`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40A -- I am a stepchild of the deceased` `my parent and the deceased` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my parent and the deceased`
    WHEN `my parent was the deceased's spouse when the deceased died` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `their marriage, civil partnership or de facto relationship lasted until my parent died, before the deceased` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 41 -- family provision`

DECLARE `Who I was to the deceased` IS ONE OF
    `the deceased's husband or wife`
    `the deceased's civil partner`
    `the deceased's de facto partner`
    `the deceased's former husband or wife, divorced`
    `the deceased's former civil partner, the civil partnership terminated`
    `the deceased's child or adopted child`
    `the child of the deceased's spouse or partner`
    `the deceased's parent`
    `someone else`

-- The facts about one applicant.
DECLARE `Family provision applicant` HAS
    `who I was`                                            IS A `Who I was to the deceased`
    `lived together for 2 years ending on the death`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `remarried or partnered before the death`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `receiving or entitled to maintenance at the death`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `my parent and the deceased`                           IS A `My parent and the deceased`
    `maintained by the deceased at the death`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `a parent of a surviving child of the deceased under 18` IS A BOOLEAN
    `under 18 at the death`                                IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN a IS A `Family provision applicant`
GIVETH A `Relationship with the deceased at the death`
`the s 5AA relationship of` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a's `who I was`
    WHEN `the deceased's husband or wife` THEN `husband or wife`
    WHEN `the deceased's civil partner` THEN `civil partner`
    WHEN `the deceased's de facto partner` THEN `de facto partner`
    WHEN `the deceased's former husband or wife, divorced` THEN `former husband or wife, divorced from the deceased`
    WHEN `the deceased's former civil partner, the civil partnership terminated` THEN `former civil partner, the civil partnership terminated under the Civil Partnerships Act 2011 s 19`
    OTHERWISE `none of these`

GIVEN a IS A `Family provision applicant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 41 -- a spouse` a IF
    `s 5AA -- I am the spouse of the deceased` (`the s 5AA relationship of` a) (a's `lived together for 2 years ending on the death`) TRUE (a's `remarried or partnered before the death`) (a's `receiving or entitled to maintenance at the death`) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 40: "child means ... any child, stepchild or adopted child".
GIVEN a IS A `Family provision applicant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 41 -- a child` a IF
    CONSIDER a's `who I was`
    WHEN `the deceased's child or adopted child` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the child of the deceased's spouse or partner` THEN `s 40A -- I am a stepchild of the deceased` (a's `my parent and the deceased`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN a IS A `Family provision applicant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 41 -- a dependant` a IF
    `s 40 -- I am a dependant of the deceased` (a's `maintained by the deceased at the death`) (`is the deceased's parent`) (a's `a parent of a surviving child of the deceased under 18`) (a's `under 18 at the death`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `is the deceased's parent` MEANS a's `who I was` EQUALS `the deceased's parent`

-- s 41(1): the court may order provision "on application by or on behalf of the said spouse, child or dependant". A
-- grant limited in its own wording: NOTHING outside it (fork F10).
GIVEN a IS A `Family provision applicant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(1) -- I may apply for family provision` a MEANS
    IF `s 41 -- a spouse` a OR `s 41 -- a child` a OR `s 41 -- a dependant` a
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: a grant limited in its own wording; the case falls outside it

-- s 41(8): "Unless the court otherwise directs, no application shall be heard by the court ... unless the proceedings
-- for such application be instituted within 9 months after the death of the deceased".
GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 41(8) -- the last day to start a family provision application` `the day of death` MEANS `the day` 9 `months after` `the day of death`

GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE, `the day of starting` IS A DATE, `the court directs otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(8) -- my application may be heard` `the day of death` `the day of starting` `the court directs otherwise` MEANS
    IF `a step on` `the day of starting` `is in time for the last day` (`s 41(8) -- the last day to start a family provision application` `the day of death`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the court directs otherwise`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The court's view and the other facts that decide whether an order may be made for an applicant.
DECLARE `Family provision hearing` HAS
    `the day of death`                                      IS A DATE
    `the day the application was started`                   IS A DATE
    `the court directs that a late application be heard`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `adequate provision was not made for my proper maintenance and support` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court is satisfied provision for me as a dependant is proper` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court refuses because of my character, conduct or circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I need a declaration of paternity`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have obtained the declaration of paternity`          IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 41(1): an order may be made where "adequate provision is not made from the estate for the proper maintenance and
-- support" of the applicant; (1A) "the court shall not make an order in respect of a dependant unless it is satisfied
-- ... that it is proper that some provision should be made"; (2)(c) the court may refuse a person whose "character or
-- conduct" disentitles them or whose "circumstances are such as make such refusal reasonable"; (8) the time limit; (9) an
-- application that needs a declaration of paternity "shall not be proceeded with until" it is obtained. Each a condition
-- or flat negative: JUST FALSE when it fails. (1A) is applied only to an applicant who is a dependant and neither a
-- spouse nor a child (fork F11). The court's judgments are inputs; the answer is "the court may order provision", never
-- that it will, or how much.
GIVEN a IS A `Family provision applicant`, h IS A `Family provision hearing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41 -- the court may order provision for me` a h MEANS
    IF `s 41(1) -- I may apply for family provision` a EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: a grant limited in its own wording; the case falls outside it
    ELSE IF `s 41(8) -- my application may be heard` (h's `the day of death`) (h's `the day the application was started`) (h's `the court directs that a late application be heard`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF h's `I need a declaration of paternity` AND (NOT h's `I have obtained the declaration of paternity`)
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE IF (NOT h's `adequate provision was not made for my proper maintenance and support`)
                   THEN JUST FALSE
                   ELSE IF `only a dependant` AND (NOT h's `the court is satisfied provision for me as a dependant is proper`)
                        THEN JUST FALSE
                        ELSE IF h's `the court refuses because of my character, conduct or circumstances`
                             THEN JUST FALSE
                             ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `only a dependant` MEANS (NOT `s 41 -- a spouse` a) AND (NOT `s 41 -- a child` a)

-- s 41(12) and s 5B: the estate an order can reach includes property the deceased gave away as a donatio mortis causa
-- (a gift made in contemplation of death) and property over which the deceased had a general power of appointment by
-- will. The values are net of debts, as the asker states them.
GIVEN `the estate` IS A NUMBER, `gifts in contemplation of death` IS A NUMBER, `property under a general power of appointment by will` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ss 5B, 41(12) -- the estate for family provision` `the estate` `gifts in contemplation of death` `property under a general power of appointment by will` MEANS
    `the estate` PLUS `gifts in contemplation of death` PLUS `property under a general power of appointment by will`

§§ `s 44 -- distribution by the personal representative`

-- The facts about one distribution, from the seat of a person who may apply under Part 4.
DECLARE `The distribution` HAS
    `the day of death`                                      IS A DATE
    `the day of distribution`                               IS A DATE
    `it was properly made`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was for the maintenance of the spouse or a dependent child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I had notified in writing that I consent or will not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the personal representative had signed written notice of any application or intended application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the personal representative had written notice that the application was started, or was served with it` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Builds the facts of one distribution from plain facts, in the order of the record.
GIVEN `death` IS A DATE, `distribution` IS A DATE, `proper` IS A BOOLEAN, `maintenance` IS A BOOLEAN, `consent` IS A BOOLEAN, `claim notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `started notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The distribution`
`the distribution facts` `death` `distribution` `proper` `maintenance` `consent` `claim notice` `started notice` MEANS
    `The distribution` WITH
        `the day of death`                                      IS `death`
        `the day of distribution`                               IS `distribution`
        `it was properly made`                                  IS `proper`
        `it was for the maintenance of the spouse or a dependent child` IS `maintenance`
        `I had notified in writing that I consent or will not apply` IS `consent`
        `the personal representative had signed written notice of any application or intended application` IS `claim notice`
        `the personal representative had written notice that the application was started, or was served with it` IS `started notice`

-- s 44(1): "No action shall lie against the personal representative ... and no application or order under this part
-- shall disturb the distribution, if it was properly made ... for the purpose of providing for the maintenance or support
-- of the spouse or any child of the deceased ... dependent on the deceased". (2): no action by a person who notified in
-- writing that they consent or will not apply. (3): no action if the distribution was properly made "(a) not earlier
-- than 6 months after the deceased's death and without notice of any application or intended application ...; or (b)
-- if notice ... has been received -- not earlier than 9 months after the deceased's death, unless the personal
-- representative receives written notice that the application has been commenced in the court or is served". (4): the
-- notice is in writing, signed. "not earlier than N months after" is read as on or after the day N months after the
-- death (fork F12). (3)(a) bars the 6-month protection on notice of "any" application, so notice signed by any
-- claimant on the estate (or their solicitor), not only by me, moves it to 9 months. Answers whether I can still sue the personal representative over the distribution: JUST FALSE where
-- the section protects it (a flat negative); NOTHING otherwise (NOTHING-kind: silent; the section protects, it does not
-- give an action).
GIVEN d IS A `The distribution`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44 -- I can sue the personal representative over the distribution` d MEANS
    IF (NOT d's `it was properly made`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: silent; the section protects only a distribution properly made
    ELSE IF d's `it was for the maintenance of the spouse or a dependent child` OR d's `I had notified in writing that I consent or will not apply` OR `protected by s 44(3)`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: silent; the section protects, it does not give an action
    WHERE
        `protected by s 44(3)` MEANS
            IF (NOT d's `the personal representative had signed written notice of any application or intended application`)
            THEN `on or after` 6
            ELSE `on or after` 9 AND (NOT d's `the personal representative had written notice that the application was started, or was served with it`)
        `on or after` n MEANS (NOT (d's `the day of distribution` `falls before` (`the day` n `months after` (d's `the day of death`))))

GIVEN d IS A `The distribution`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(1) -- the distribution can be disturbed by a family provision order` d MEANS
    IF d's `it was properly made` AND d's `it was for the maintenance of the spouse or a dependent child`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: silent; only s 44(1) speaks of disturbing a distribution

§§ `s 65 -- deaths in an uncertain order`

DECLARE `Who is taken to have survived` IS ONE OF
    `the first person, the younger, is taken to have survived the second by 1 day`
    `the second person, the younger, is taken to have survived the first by 1 day`
    `s 65 does not apply`
    `not answered: they were born on the same day`

-- s 65: where 2 or more persons have died "in circumstances rendering it uncertain which of them survived the other",
-- the deaths are presumed "(subject to any order of the court)" to have occurred "in order of seniority, and accordingly
-- the younger shall be deemed to have survived the elder for a period of 1 day". Persons born on the same day: seniority
-- turns on facts not asked (fork F13).
GIVEN `it is uncertain who survived` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN, `the first person's birth day` IS A DATE, `the second person's birth day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Who is taken to have survived`
`s 65 -- who is taken to have survived` `it is uncertain who survived` `the court has ordered otherwise` `the first person's birth day` `the second person's birth day` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is uncertain who survived`) OR `the court has ordered otherwise`
    THEN `s 65 does not apply`
    ELSE IF `the first person's birth day` `falls after` `the second person's birth day`
         THEN `the first person, the younger, is taken to have survived the second by 1 day`
         ELSE IF `the second person's birth day` `falls after` `the first person's birth day`
              THEN `the second person, the younger, is taken to have survived the first by 1 day`
              ELSE `not answered: they were born on the same day`

§§ `s 66 -- actions that survive a death`

DECLARE `Kind of damages` IS ONE OF
    `damages for pain and suffering, bodily or mental harm, or curtailment of expectation of life`
    `exemplary damages`
    `the deceased's probable future earnings had they survived`
    `a loss or gain to the estate because of the death, other than funeral expenses`
    `funeral expenses`
    `other damages, such as medical expenses or earnings lost before the death`

-- The facts about the deceased's cause of action.
DECLARE `The surviving action` HAS
    `it is for defamation or seduction`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the death was caused by the act or omission sued on`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is for personal injury from a dust-related condition` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injury results from tobacco`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deceased started a proceeding before dying`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the condition caused or contributed to the death`     IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 66(1): "with the exception of causes of action for defamation or seduction", causes of action vested in a person
-- survive for the benefit of the estate. (2): the damages "(a) shall not include damages for pain and suffering, for any
-- bodily or mental harm or for curtailment of expectation of life; and (b) shall not include exemplary damages; ... (d)
-- where the death has been caused by the act or omission ... shall be calculated without reference to -- (i) loss or
-- gain to the estate consequent upon the death save that a sum in respect of funeral expenses may be included; or (ii)
-- future probable earnings". (2A): (2)(a) damages may be recovered if the action relates to personal injury from a
-- dust-related condition, the deceased started a proceeding before dying, and the condition caused or contributed to
-- the death; (2B): not injury from tobacco. Flat negatives: JUST FALSE. The defamation and seduction exception is
-- answered JUST FALSE (fork F14). (2)(c), breach of promise to marry, is out.
GIVEN `the damages` IS A `Kind of damages`, s IS A `The surviving action`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66 -- the estate can recover` `the damages` s MEANS
    IF s's `it is for defamation or seduction`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the damages`
         WHEN `damages for pain and suffering, bodily or mental harm, or curtailment of expectation of life` THEN
             IF s's `it is for personal injury from a dust-related condition` AND (NOT s's `the injury results from tobacco`) AND s's `the deceased started a proceeding before dying` AND s's `the condition caused or contributed to the death`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE
         WHEN `exemplary damages` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `funeral expenses` THEN
             IF s's `the death was caused by the act or omission sued on`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: silent; s 66(2)(d) speaks only where the act caused the death
         WHEN `other damages, such as medical expenses or earnings lost before the death` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE
             IF s's `the death was caused by the act or omission sued on`
             THEN JUST FALSE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: silent; s 66(2)(d) speaks only where the act caused the death

-- s 66(6): an action that survives against an estate "may be brought against any beneficiary to whom any part of the
-- estate has been distributed"; (9): "In no case may a judgment against a beneficiary exceed the amount of the
-- distribution made to the beneficiary." The (7) contribution and indemnity and the (8) equitable defences are left to
-- the court.
GIVEN `a part of the estate was distributed to me` IS A BOOLEAN, `the amount distributed to me` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 66(6), (9) -- the most a judgment against me can be` `a part of the estate was distributed to me` `the amount distributed to me` MEANS
    IF `a part of the estate was distributed to me`
    THEN JUST `the amount distributed to me`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: a grant limited in its own wording (s 66(6) reaches only a beneficiary who received a distribution)
